kubeos-network (1.9.1-7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Debian revision numbering: 1.9.1-1kubeos7 -> 1.9.1-7. The revision is a plain Debian one now
    instead of the 1kubeosN prefix the first uploads used; the upstream version is
    unchanged. The KubeOS distribution version lives in kubeos-base, which is 0.2.0.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * kubeos-coredns.service: condition on /etc/kubernetes/coredns.conf instead of
    /etc/coredns/Corefile. The Corefile is generated at first boot and survives
    `kubeadm reset`, so a machine that later joined another cluster as a worker satisfied
    the condition, the shipped .wants link started it at boot, and it restarted every 5 s
    for ever ("stat /etc/kubernetes/coredns.conf: no such file or directory") - a failed
    unit and a journal full of errors on every worker, measured on kubeos3 on 2026-11-20.
    The kubeconfig only exists where a control plane ran, so a worker now skips the unit.
    Note that `systemctl is-enabled` said "disabled" all along: the vendor .wants link
    starts the unit at boot regardless, so that output is not evidence that a unit on a
    worker never runs.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:40:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dh_installsystemd gets --no-enable only, not --no-start. --no-start also stops the
    units during an upgrade and never starts them again: upgrading this package took the
    whole control plane down (all eight units inactive, kubectl refused on :6443), measured
    on the live node on 2026-11-19. --no-enable alone is what was needed - it stops the
    package from enabling units (flanneld above all), while the normal stop/start around a
    binary upgrade keeps the cluster running.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Stop dh_installsystemd from enabling and starting/restarting units by itself. It
    were enabling flanneld.service - which hook 9050 documents as never-to-enable, since
    it cannot run as a host service - and it restarted units on every upgrade, including
    control-plane units that must not start before node-setup has written the PKI. The
    .wants links shipped in the package now decide, and nothing else.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:20:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Stop shipping the CNI plugins. /opt/cni/bin already belongs to kubernetes-cni,
    which the kubelet package depends on at the same upstream version, so dpkg refused
    the package a second time: "trying to overwrite '/opt/cni/bin/bridge', which is
    also in package kubernetes-cni". Depend on it instead of duplicating it - 27 MB
    smaller, and one owner per path.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:45:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ship /etc/modules-load.d/kubeos.conf instead of overwriting
    /etc/modules-load.d/modules.conf. That file belongs to the systemd package, so dpkg
    refused to install this one at all: "trying to overwrite '/etc/modules-load.d/
    modules.conf', which is also in package systemd". Found by installing the archive on
    a live node - the ISO used to overwrite the file because includes.chroot is copied
    after the package install, which is exactly a problem packaging has to solve properly.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:35:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ship the unit enablement as a package file. Build hook 9050 called
    systemctl enable for these units, which a package must not do: it aborts a
    chroot build (the trap documented in that hook). A .wants symlink owned by
    dpkg is the same declaration, so a node installed from the archive alone
    comes up identically.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0530

kubeos-network (1.9.1-1kubeos1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging. CNI plugins v1.9.1, flanneld v0.28.10 and CoreDNS v1.14.6,
    the same artefacts build hook 9026 fetched, now dpkg-owned and in /usr/bin and
    /opt/cni/bin instead of /usr/local/bin.

